<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n279" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăbȳdus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăbȳdos</span></b> , i (in
		MSS. also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aboedus</span></b> ), f.
			(m., <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1, 207</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄβυδος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Mysia</i>, <i>on the
				narrowest point of the Hellespont</i>, <i>opposite
				Sestos</i>, now perh. <i>Aidos</i> or <i>Avido</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 9, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Auct.
					Her. 4, 54, 68</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostrifer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 207</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					H. 18, 127</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">19, 30 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Abydum oppidum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 32, 40, § 141</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence
			deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăbȳdēnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>belonging to
			Abydus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvenis, i. e. Leander,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 1, 2, 87</span></i>
			; the same <i>absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Abydenus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					18, 1</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăbȳdēni</span></b> , <i>the inhabitants of Abydus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 31,
			16</span></i>.</div>
